WEBVTT

00:00:31.890 --> 00:00:35.090
Enemy at 10 o'clock high!
Take evasive action! Evasive action!

00:01:02.760 --> 00:01:04.460
Calling Area 88 headquarters.

00:01:04.460 --> 00:01:08.920
Anti-government artillery units moving northward
from southern division, point 3B!

00:01:09.230 --> 00:01:12.200
This is Shin Kazama, zero-zero section.

00:01:12.200 --> 00:01:14.570
This is Kazama from zero-zero section.

00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:17.310
Damn!

00:01:17.310 --> 00:01:19.310
Do they hear me or not?

00:01:19.310 --> 00:01:21.810
It's the ususal bullshit.

00:01:21.810 --> 00:01:23.680
In any case, they'd better keep
their hands off my prey!

00:02:08.160 --> 00:02:10.180
There's about $6000 earned.

00:02:27.040 --> 00:02:29.840
Runway in sight. Wing angle at 7 degrees.

00:02:35.380 --> 00:02:37.480
Leading edge slot open.

00:02:39.020 --> 00:02:40.460
Flaperons at 30 degrees.

00:02:43.960 --> 00:02:45.550
Air brakes engaged.

00:02:48.100 --> 00:02:49.230
Landing gear down.

00:02:49.230 --> 00:02:51.200
Commencing approach!

00:05:29.190 --> 00:05:31.830
Whoa, right there, just hold that pose!

00:05:31.830 --> 00:05:34.900
A lone samurai, who braves the days
upon hot and sandy battlefields.

00:05:34.900 --> 00:05:37.090
You got a good face, man!

00:05:39.630 --> 00:05:41.000
You're Japanese, are you?

00:05:41.000 --> 00:05:43.640
I'll bet it's been a while since you've
seen another Japanese.

00:05:43.640 --> 00:05:46.980
I'm Goh Mutsuki from N.P. Broadcasting.

00:05:46.980 --> 00:05:48.310
Mutsuki?

00:05:48.310 --> 00:05:50.970
Folks call me Rocky. I'd like it if you would too.

00:05:52.210 --> 00:05:55.740
That's enough. I don't like having
my picture taken.

00:05:55.980 --> 00:05:58.950
Now that's just cold. This is my job, man!

00:05:59.350 --> 00:06:02.690
Then I think that's a subject you'd like.

00:06:05.930 --> 00:06:07.300
It's on fire!

00:06:07.300 --> 00:06:09.360
That's Greg's Skyhawk.

00:06:33.320 --> 00:06:35.550
Hurry up and put that fire out!

00:06:37.090 --> 00:06:39.990
Hey, McCoy! Is old man McCoy here?!

00:06:40.200 --> 00:06:41.420
What happened? You all right?!

00:06:44.230 --> 00:06:45.330
Comin'!

00:06:45.330 --> 00:06:46.840
I took a shot right through my windscreen.

00:06:46.840 --> 00:06:49.300
I had shards bouncin' around in my helmet!

00:06:51.410 --> 00:06:53.740
Guess you'll be needin' some alcohol.

00:06:53.740 --> 00:06:55.730
'Preciate it!

00:06:58.080 --> 00:06:59.950
Ya gotta value yer life, right?

00:06:59.950 --> 00:07:02.450
Value your life, and it'll last you a whole lifetime.

00:07:02.450 --> 00:07:06.720
Damn, that stings!

00:07:06.720 --> 00:07:08.850
It's even stronger than hair tonic!

00:07:10.390 --> 00:07:11.220
Here!

00:07:11.890 --> 00:07:14.860
All right, fill 'er up! I'm heading back out again!

00:07:14.860 --> 00:07:16.700
There's a whole frickin' swarm of tanks out there!

00:07:17.130 --> 00:07:18.600
But they just got done putting out the fire!

00:07:18.600 --> 00:07:20.900
He's going out again without even
doing any repairs?!

00:07:46.330 --> 00:07:50.270
Goddammit! How the hell could you break down
on me now after coming so far?!

00:07:51.630 --> 00:07:53.400
Bucksey, you suck!

00:07:53.400 --> 00:07:56.100
Man, you were born under the
unluckiest star out there!

00:07:56.100 --> 00:07:58.840
Value the plane above yer own life, dammit!

00:07:59.140 --> 00:08:01.310
Shut the hell up, you scraggly-faced,
bearded Buddha!

00:08:01.310 --> 00:08:02.840
Bucksey!

00:08:02.840 --> 00:08:05.210
Your plane's done for.

00:08:05.210 --> 00:08:09.650
Aw, it hasn't even been a month since
I bought the damn thing!

00:08:13.020 --> 00:08:15.750
I've covered lots of stories as far as
Vietnam and Africa,

00:08:15.860 --> 00:08:17.590
but never anything this crazy.

00:08:17.590 --> 00:08:19.860
You look pretty shocked.

00:08:19.860 --> 00:08:22.160
This is the norm around here.

00:08:23.160 --> 00:08:24.330
Hey...

00:09:12.350 --> 00:09:15.110
Two years and three months more...

00:09:15.780 --> 00:09:17.510
Two years, huh?

00:09:39.270 --> 00:09:43.210
It's too long! Way too long!

00:09:43.210 --> 00:09:46.650
I've had enough of murdering people!

00:09:48.150 --> 00:09:50.890
I want to go back to Japan.

00:09:50.890 --> 00:09:54.220
I want to go back alive and
walk on Japanese soil!

00:09:57.790 --> 00:10:06.860
One, two! One, two! One, two!

00:10:11.310 --> 00:10:14.870
The both of you have truly outstanding
academic records.

00:10:15.210 --> 00:10:20.310
There is nothing more to teach you
here at this flight school.

00:10:21.320 --> 00:10:24.390
From here on, I want you to work hard
and get more experience

00:10:24.390 --> 00:10:27.050
so that you'll be able to fly the skies
all over our world.

00:10:41.970 --> 00:10:43.370
Ryoko...

00:10:44.510 --> 00:10:47.530
I'll be back in Japan the day
after tomorrow, okay?

00:10:52.380 --> 00:10:53.580
Hey, Shin!

00:10:53.580 --> 00:10:54.880
Whatcha doing?

00:10:55.550 --> 00:10:56.680
I might have known!

00:10:56.680 --> 00:11:00.890
You just can't wait to get back and see
your Ryoko, can ya?

00:11:00.890 --> 00:11:02.090
No, I...

00:11:02.090 --> 00:11:03.260
Well now!

00:11:03.260 --> 00:11:06.290
You won the heart of the daughter of
Yamato Airline's president...

00:11:06.290 --> 00:11:08.000
It sure is enough to make a guy jealous!

00:11:08.000 --> 00:11:10.430
You're headed straight for the good life, buddy.

00:11:10.430 --> 00:11:12.500
Kanzaki! That's not what I'm thinking at all.

00:11:12.500 --> 00:11:15.000
Don't be silly, I'm just messing with you!

00:11:15.000 --> 00:11:18.340
We aren't even thinking about
marriage at this point.

00:11:18.610 --> 00:11:21.640
Right now the flying takes all I've got.

00:11:21.640 --> 00:11:25.250
Well, maybe your lack of greed
is the best thing about you.

00:11:25.250 --> 00:11:29.520
As for me, I'll take advantage of whatever I can.

00:11:29.520 --> 00:11:32.010
I admire your drive.

00:11:32.590 --> 00:11:37.530
Well, in any case it looks like we're on the
fast-track to being Yamato Airlines' top pilots.

00:11:38.390 --> 00:11:39.520
C'mon!

00:11:39.630 --> 00:11:42.830
Today's a big day! Let's go get hammered
and celebrate!

00:11:42.830 --> 00:11:44.230
Sure, let's go paint the town red!

00:11:46.070 --> 00:11:48.500
Ah, man, I feel great!

00:11:49.400 --> 00:11:50.940
All right! Off to the next bar!

00:11:50.940 --> 00:11:52.410
Yeah!

00:11:52.410 --> 00:11:55.070
Just bring me a beer or a whiskey or whatever!

00:11:56.280 --> 00:11:59.810
Another two days and it's, "Goodbye, Paris!"

00:12:09.790 --> 00:12:11.190
Hey, Shin.

00:12:11.190 --> 00:12:12.990
Wake up and sign this.

00:12:13.360 --> 00:12:13.930
C'mon.

00:12:13.930 --> 00:12:14.030
Lemme sleep...
C'mon.

00:12:14.030 --> 00:12:15.460
Lemme sleep...

00:12:16.900 --> 00:12:19.900
I'll let you sleep as long as you want
once you've signed this.

00:12:19.900 --> 00:12:21.900
This is the paperwork for staying outside
the dorm overnight.

00:12:21.900 --> 00:12:23.300
Come on, hurry up and sign it.

00:12:23.300 --> 00:12:26.640
Huh? Paperwork for staying out?

00:12:26.940 --> 00:12:31.380
That's right. This is gonna be
an all-nighter after all.

00:12:31.950 --> 00:12:33.070
Right...

00:12:52.230 --> 00:12:53.930
Atta boy.

00:12:58.770 --> 00:13:00.300
Farewell, Shin.

00:13:50.860 --> 00:13:52.330
Hey!

00:13:52.330 --> 00:13:53.990
Wake up!

00:13:59.570 --> 00:14:02.840
You're Shin Kazama, right?

00:14:02.840 --> 00:14:04.840
Who are you?

00:14:04.840 --> 00:14:07.110
You're coming with us.

00:14:07.110 --> 00:14:10.350
You've made a contract with us.

00:14:10.350 --> 00:14:12.110
What do you mean, contract?

00:14:12.110 --> 00:14:13.880
Are you sure this isn't some kind of mistake?

00:14:13.880 --> 00:14:16.480
I'm a Yamato Airlines trainee
studying abroad here.

00:14:16.480 --> 00:14:19.090
As of 12:00 this morning,

00:14:19.090 --> 00:14:24.320
you have resigned your post at Yamato Airlines,
and joined our country, Aslan's, foreign legion.

00:14:26.690 --> 00:14:29.600
Yeah, whatever. Don't be ridiculous!

00:14:34.740 --> 00:14:36.900
This is your signature.

00:14:37.340 --> 00:14:40.070
As stipulated in the contract,
for the next three years...

00:14:40.070 --> 00:14:44.250
You will serve in the kingdom
of Aslan's air force.

00:14:44.250 --> 00:14:46.010
This is ridiculous!

00:14:51.620 --> 00:14:53.820
Mr. Kazama...

00:14:53.820 --> 00:14:57.020
Do you want to be shot as a deserter?

00:14:58.090 --> 00:15:00.820
I don't recall enlisting in any foreign legion!

00:15:02.100 --> 00:15:03.800
"Hey, Shin."

00:15:03.800 --> 00:15:05.500
"This is the paperwork for staying outside
the dorm overnight."

00:15:05.500 --> 00:15:07.200
"Sign it."

00:15:07.470 --> 00:15:08.600
"Sign it!"

00:15:08.970 --> 00:15:10.170
"SIGN IT!"

00:15:10.170 --> 00:15:11.840
Kanzaki?!

00:15:11.840 --> 00:15:14.670
Why... Why?

00:15:16.010 --> 00:15:17.500
WHY?!

00:15:28.220 --> 00:15:31.460
Hi! I could hear you in here. Mind if I come in?

00:15:31.460 --> 00:15:33.220
Nah...

00:15:35.600 --> 00:15:37.270
Hey, what's going on?

00:15:37.270 --> 00:15:39.030
Nothing.

00:15:47.540 --> 00:15:50.850
Would you talk to me about Japan?

00:15:50.850 --> 00:15:52.410
Just for a little while...

00:15:52.410 --> 00:15:55.150
Stories about Japan? Well, the only thing is...

00:15:55.150 --> 00:15:58.120
For the past three years, I haven't been
back to Japan either.

00:15:58.120 --> 00:16:00.120
See, our head office is in England,

00:16:00.120 --> 00:16:02.320
and so I've been working in Europe
for a long time.

00:16:02.320 --> 00:16:04.690
Is that right?

00:16:05.590 --> 00:16:07.360
Do you have any family in Japan?

00:16:08.130 --> 00:16:09.530
None!

00:16:10.000 --> 00:16:11.630
They abroad?

00:16:11.630 --> 00:16:15.030
I haven't had any family since
the day I was born.

00:16:15.400 --> 00:16:17.740
I never even knew my own mother's face.

00:16:20.170 --> 00:16:23.300
I see... Sorry, I shouldn't have asked.

00:16:27.320 --> 00:16:31.950
It's comforting just being able to
see another Japanese.

00:16:42.030 --> 00:16:43.530
Rocky?

00:16:43.530 --> 00:16:48.700
I am Saki Vashtar, lieutenant colonel
of the Aslan Royal Air Force.

00:16:48.700 --> 00:16:51.470
And the highest in command at this base, right?

00:16:51.470 --> 00:16:53.530
Pleased to make your acquaintance!

00:16:53.770 --> 00:16:56.400
What is a Japanese like you doing here?

00:16:58.350 --> 00:17:01.320
Well, this is the only foreign legion
air force there is.

00:17:01.320 --> 00:17:04.650
Plus I heard there was a Japanese pilot here.

00:17:04.650 --> 00:17:06.890
Are you speaking of Shin Kazama?

00:17:06.890 --> 00:17:09.190
I have already met him, you know.

00:17:11.960 --> 00:17:15.200
All right, Rocky, I'll let you do your
story on this base,

00:17:15.200 --> 00:17:18.690
but know that these are the very frontlines of
Hell. Your safety is by no means guaranteed.

00:17:20.230 --> 00:17:21.370
Roger!

00:17:21.370 --> 00:17:25.410
For supplies, you should go visit McCoy's
storehouse at the far side of the hangar.

00:17:25.410 --> 00:17:27.430
I imagine he'll have what you need.

00:17:28.080 --> 00:17:29.580
Does he have film too?

00:17:29.580 --> 00:17:31.980
He sells toilet paper, warheads...

00:17:33.650 --> 00:17:34.780
And everything in between.

00:17:48.000 --> 00:17:49.800
Hey, old McCoy!

00:17:49.800 --> 00:17:51.970
Ah, it's the reporter from earlier.

00:17:51.970 --> 00:17:54.140
I figured you'd be along sooner or later.

00:17:54.140 --> 00:17:55.400
Huh?

00:17:55.400 --> 00:17:57.970
Oh, I was just thinking out loud.

00:17:57.970 --> 00:18:01.110
Gimme about 50 rolls of 35mm Tri-Ex.

00:18:01.110 --> 00:18:02.700
Sure thing.

00:18:03.510 --> 00:18:06.680
Do reporters these days usually go cover
stories without even bringing film?

00:18:06.680 --> 00:18:07.620
And you are?

00:18:07.620 --> 00:18:09.980
The name's Mickey. Pleased to meet ya.

00:18:11.790 --> 00:18:13.850
What, haven't you outgrown
the fear of strangers yet?

00:18:13.850 --> 00:18:15.090
As for my film,

00:18:15.090 --> 00:18:16.360
in the confusion after that accident earlier today,

00:18:16.360 --> 00:18:19.630
I ended up leaving my film bag sitting
out in the blazing hot sun.

00:18:19.630 --> 00:18:21.760
Two hundred rolls up in smoke!

00:18:21.760 --> 00:18:24.360
Mistakes can cost you your life around here, pal.

00:18:24.730 --> 00:18:26.830
So are you also one of Shin's buddies?

00:18:26.830 --> 00:18:28.740
What about him?

00:18:28.740 --> 00:18:31.270
Something about him kinda bugs me.

00:18:31.270 --> 00:18:34.840
I've spent years going around from
battlefield to battlefield,

00:18:34.840 --> 00:18:37.450
so I can tell you that he certainly doesn't
have the eyes of a soldier.

00:18:37.450 --> 00:18:39.280
He's just not like you guys.

00:18:39.280 --> 00:18:41.650
Pretty sharp there, mister reporter.

00:18:41.650 --> 00:18:46.120
Shin's not like Mickey here. He's not
at war because he likes it.

00:18:46.120 --> 00:18:47.560
You mean you know?

00:18:47.560 --> 00:18:49.860
The men around here come from all kinds
of different backgrounds.

00:18:49.860 --> 00:18:53.030
But there's not a one who'll actually
talk about his past.

00:18:53.030 --> 00:18:54.260
I'll bet.

00:18:54.260 --> 00:18:55.330
Here.

00:18:55.330 --> 00:18:56.730
Thanks.

00:18:56.730 --> 00:18:59.800
There's still another 300 rolls.
If you run out, come back anytime.

00:18:59.800 --> 00:19:01.790
You're a lifesaver.

00:19:02.370 --> 00:19:06.010
Lessee... 50 rolls of film...

00:19:06.010 --> 00:19:09.010
Huh... You treat the outsiders well
enough, don't ya, Pops?

00:19:09.010 --> 00:19:10.240
Like hell!

00:19:10.240 --> 00:19:14.250
I'm the one who left his bag sitting in the sun.

00:19:14.250 --> 00:19:17.410
I made out like a bandit on this one!

00:19:17.620 --> 00:19:18.880
Huh?!

00:19:31.230 --> 00:19:33.900
Are those the new recruits flying
in formation up there?

00:19:33.900 --> 00:19:36.000
Those are BAC Lightnings.

00:19:36.000 --> 00:19:38.730
They've brought in some more frickin'
old planes to fight with.

00:20:10.140 --> 00:20:13.840
They went broke fighting in an African civil war,
so they drifted here.

00:20:24.620 --> 00:20:26.140
Cut it out!

00:20:26.990 --> 00:20:28.820
We're not on display here.

00:20:28.820 --> 00:20:31.060
I'll smash that damn camera.

00:20:31.060 --> 00:20:32.090
What was that?

00:20:32.090 --> 00:20:34.390
Give it a rest!

00:20:39.200 --> 00:20:40.770
Hey, McCoy, where's Shin?

00:20:40.770 --> 00:20:45.340
Ah, right, he went out on the afternoon sortie.
He's not back yet.

00:20:45.340 --> 00:20:46.840
What did you say?!

00:20:46.840 --> 00:20:50.580
I think he went out on a mission last night too.

00:20:50.580 --> 00:20:52.210
That's pretty amazing.

00:20:52.210 --> 00:20:54.610
Why don't you try to be more like him?

00:20:55.080 --> 00:20:56.880
Hey, Saki!

00:20:58.550 --> 00:20:59.990
This ain't funny, man!

00:20:59.990 --> 00:21:03.260
Why don't you stop Shin from going out?
You're working him to death!

00:21:03.260 --> 00:21:04.360
Listen, Mickey.

00:21:04.360 --> 00:21:08.960
Around here, it is entirely up to the pilot which
missions he wants to participate in.

00:21:08.960 --> 00:21:11.130
It's not my place to step in.

00:21:11.130 --> 00:21:12.690
But...

00:21:13.470 --> 00:21:16.100
In order to get out of Area 88,

00:21:16.100 --> 00:21:18.770
a pilot must survive three years of combat,

00:21:18.770 --> 00:21:21.780
pay a penalty of 1.5 million dollars,

00:21:21.780 --> 00:21:23.580
or...

00:21:23.580 --> 00:21:25.170
He can desert.

00:21:29.280 --> 00:21:33.690
Shin should have $1.5 million very shortly.

00:22:23.570 --> 00:22:24.910
Sunset...

00:22:24.910 --> 00:22:28.600
To me it's the same crimson as blood.

00:22:39.650 --> 00:22:41.950
Okay, I guess that about wraps it up, huh?

00:22:42.460 --> 00:22:44.220
Everything looks normal in the
engine compartment too.

00:22:44.330 --> 00:22:45.890
I think that should be good enough.

00:22:45.890 --> 00:22:47.900
Let's have our supervisor come and look it over.

00:22:47.900 --> 00:22:49.760
Sure.

00:22:49.760 --> 00:22:51.320
I'll go get him.

00:22:54.030 --> 00:22:56.970
AUTHORIZED
PERSONNEL ONLY

00:22:59.870 --> 00:23:03.110
I've been searching for you!
What are you doing here?

00:23:07.680 --> 00:23:09.280
These.

00:23:09.280 --> 00:23:11.820
Hurry up and carry them over there, all right?

00:23:11.820 --> 00:23:13.250
Huh?

00:23:36.410 --> 00:23:37.480
Well, there you go.

00:23:37.480 --> 00:23:39.480
I'd like you to load them up too.

00:23:39.480 --> 00:23:40.470
Huh?

00:23:41.480 --> 00:23:43.250
Okay, I'll do that.

00:23:43.620 --> 00:23:44.990
Ryoko!

00:23:44.990 --> 00:23:46.350
Ah, Papa!

00:23:46.350 --> 00:23:49.360
My usual assistant isn't here.

00:23:49.360 --> 00:23:50.260
What?!

00:23:50.260 --> 00:23:51.590
Then...

00:23:52.130 --> 00:23:56.260
Well, actually I'm a flight academy student.
My name is Kazama.

00:23:56.260 --> 00:24:01.000
I... I'm so sorry! I had no idea.

00:24:03.300 --> 00:24:05.110
Please excuse my daughter.

00:24:05.110 --> 00:24:07.940
My name is Tsugumo. I'm with Yamato Airlines.

00:24:28.500 --> 00:24:29.730
Are you scared, Shin?

00:24:29.730 --> 00:24:32.170
I feel like my heart's gonna do a somersault!

00:24:32.170 --> 00:24:34.940
But you're the one who wants to
be a jet pilot, right?

00:24:34.940 --> 00:24:37.340
Those planes go really fast, you know.

00:24:37.340 --> 00:24:40.310
Only speed feels a lot different
when you're in a cockpit!

00:24:59.430 --> 00:25:01.100
Ryoko...

00:25:01.100 --> 00:25:03.060
My dear angel...

00:25:25.750 --> 00:25:29.090
But I am no longer the man I once was.

00:25:29.090 --> 00:25:30.960
I have been stained by gunpowder and blood.

00:25:30.960 --> 00:25:33.990
I'm a devil incarnate, consumed by
the flames of hatred!

00:25:45.070 --> 00:25:47.540
Hey there! Shin!

00:25:50.280 --> 00:25:52.310
Glad to see you made it back
safe and sound again today.

00:25:52.310 --> 00:25:55.950
Say, I got me some secondhand Sidewinders
on the cheap. Care to purchase a few?

00:25:55.950 --> 00:25:58.650
If you keep on hawking weaponry like that,

00:25:58.650 --> 00:26:00.650
you're going to fall straight to Hell
sooner or later.

00:26:00.650 --> 00:26:04.090
Son, this is Area 88,
Hell's very own Main Street.

00:26:04.090 --> 00:26:06.830
Tell me, where do I fall from here?

00:26:06.830 --> 00:26:09.130
Good point. How much you want?

00:26:09.130 --> 00:26:11.230
That's the spirit!

00:26:11.230 --> 00:26:13.300
A thousand bucks for 50 of 'em!

00:26:13.300 --> 00:26:14.640
That's cheap!

00:26:14.640 --> 00:26:16.340
You sure they're not defective?

00:26:16.340 --> 00:26:20.310
I have never sold a single missile
that wouldn't fire...

00:26:20.310 --> 00:26:23.330
Though there have been a few that
didn't explode on contact.

00:26:28.420 --> 00:26:31.420
I'll thank you to not interfere with
my business dealings, Boris!

00:26:31.420 --> 00:26:33.050
No offense, old man,

00:26:33.050 --> 00:26:34.520
but let's just pretend this conversation
never took place.

00:26:34.520 --> 00:26:36.260
Don't be like that!

00:26:36.260 --> 00:26:39.760
What did I ever do to make you
want to ruin a sale for me?!

00:26:39.760 --> 00:26:43.060
You're haggling for money, but
it's life and death for us.

00:26:43.060 --> 00:26:45.400
Faulty equipment will cost a man his life.

00:26:45.400 --> 00:26:48.370
Well, you can go to Hell!

00:26:50.640 --> 00:26:54.310
So is it true that bastard Boris
sleeps with the light on?

00:26:54.310 --> 00:26:58.610
He says he's afraid that if he goes into the
darkness, he'll never come out again.

00:26:58.610 --> 00:27:01.150
Afraid? Well, how about that!

00:27:01.150 --> 00:27:04.520
So a man with a brutish face
like that is scared, eh?

00:27:04.520 --> 00:27:06.820
Well ha ha on him!

00:27:19.230 --> 00:27:22.230
I'll now tell you the objective of our next strike.

00:27:24.910 --> 00:27:28.780
Southern division, point 2C,
the surface-to-air missile base.

00:27:28.780 --> 00:27:31.580
You're telling us to fly right
into the Devil's mouth?!

00:27:31.580 --> 00:27:35.880
We pass even close to there and missiles
come down on us like rain!

00:27:35.880 --> 00:27:39.620
Tomorrow afternoon, the Aslan Royal Air Force
will commence an operation.

00:27:39.620 --> 00:27:44.760
In order to keep their casualties to a minimum,
it is necessary that we crush this base!

00:27:44.760 --> 00:27:48.600
So we'll be sacrificing ourselves
for the government's forces?

00:27:48.600 --> 00:27:50.860
It's always the really dangerous work
that gets handed to us.

00:27:50.860 --> 00:27:55.670
You are a foreign legion that is paid
good money by our country.

00:27:55.670 --> 00:27:57.870
Don't forget that.

00:28:00.840 --> 00:28:02.780
We will depart in two hours.

00:28:02.780 --> 00:28:04.650
If you are interested in this mission,
then speak now.

00:28:04.650 --> 00:28:06.910
Compensation will be twice the
normal rate: $20,000.

00:28:22.700 --> 00:28:28.700
Dare ga anata ni kizu wo tsuketa no
<i>Who has wounded you?</i>

00:28:28.700 --> 00:28:34.810
Wake wo tazuneta koto wa mada nai keredo
<i>I still haven't asked the reason why</i>

00:28:34.810 --> 00:28:40.810
Hitomi no blue, sabishii iro ne
<i>But the blue of your eyes is such a lonely color</i>

00:28:40.810 --> 00:28:45.220
Kokoro wa mou koko ni nai
<i>Your heart isn't here anymore</i>

00:28:45.220 --> 00:28:46.990
Make sure you take some good pictures of this!

00:28:46.990 --> 00:28:47.520
Goodbye, sweet goodbye, blue lion
<i>Goodbye, sweet goodbye, blue lion</i>

00:28:47.520 --> 00:28:50.790
This is one mission we might not
make it back from.

00:28:50.790 --> 00:28:53.060
If you don't, I'll send these to your
folks back in your country.

00:28:53.060 --> 00:28:56.790
Goodbye, sweet goodbye, blue iron
<i>Goodbye, sweet goodbye, blue iron</i>

00:28:58.630 --> 00:28:59.170
Sundown, 20:30 hours...

00:28:59.170 --> 00:29:01.000
Tsuki wa kakete wa mata michite yuku wa
<i>After the moon wanes it always waxes once again</i>

00:29:01.000 --> 00:29:01.100
<i>After the moon wanes it always waxes once again</i>
Tsuki wa kakete wa mata michite yuku wa

00:29:01.100 --> 00:29:02.200
Time to go!

00:29:02.200 --> 00:29:05.240
<i>After the moon wanes it always waxes once again</i>
Tsuki wa kakete wa mata michite yuku wa

00:29:05.240 --> 00:29:09.870
Sore wo anata ni tsugetai
<i>I want to let you know that</i>

00:29:11.410 --> 00:29:17.620
Namida nante imi ga nai
<i>"Tears are meaningless"</i>

00:29:17.620 --> 00:29:23.490
Anata no "ah" kuchiguse
<i>Your favorite saying</i>

00:29:23.490 --> 00:29:28.430
Yasashisa dake osoreteru
<i>The only thing you're afraid of is kindness</i>

00:29:28.430 --> 00:29:30.360
Control Tower to Blue-1. Take off!

00:29:30.360 --> 00:29:31.530
Dakishimete ageru yo
<i>I'll hold you close to me</i>

00:29:31.530 --> 00:29:36.030
<i>I'll hold you close to me</i>
Dakishimete ageru yo

00:29:55.790 --> 00:29:58.730
Blue-2, taxi to the runway and take off!

00:30:02.060 --> 00:30:08.300
Tsuki wa kakete wa mata michite yuku wa
<i>After the moon wanes it always waxes once again</i>

00:30:08.300 --> 00:30:13.670
Sore wo anata ni tsugetai
<i>I want to let you know that</i>

00:30:14.410 --> 00:30:21.050
Namida nante imi ga nai
<i>"Tears are meaningless"</i>

00:30:21.050 --> 00:30:26.820
Anata no "ah" kuchiguse
<i>Your favorite saying</i>

00:30:26.820 --> 00:30:32.690
Yasashisa dake osoreteru
<i>The only thing you're afraid of is kindness</i>

00:30:33.230 --> 00:30:39.060
Dakishimete ageru yo
<i>I'll hold you close to me</i>

00:30:58.350 --> 00:31:02.120
Shin! Do you think the enemy will
send up any fighters?

00:31:02.120 --> 00:31:03.660
Couldn't tell you.

00:31:03.660 --> 00:31:07.330
After all, today's target is a supply base
with anti-aircraft missile emplacements.

00:31:07.330 --> 00:31:09.760
From a common-sense standpoint,

00:31:09.760 --> 00:31:12.760
maybe we should assume they wouldn't need
fighters since they have anti-aircraft missiles.

00:31:19.270 --> 00:31:21.680
We'll soon be within the enemy's
defensive perimeter.

00:31:21.680 --> 00:31:24.240
If we don't reduce our altitude,
we'll be missile fodder!

00:31:34.490 --> 00:31:36.190
Target in sight.

00:31:36.190 --> 00:31:37.710
We're going to proceed with a
low-altitude attack!

00:31:38.890 --> 00:31:41.990
That big-ass supply carrier is mine!

00:31:42.530 --> 00:31:45.430
Like hell! That thing is mine!

00:31:45.430 --> 00:31:47.370
Attack!

00:31:59.010 --> 00:31:59.880
Enemy fighters detected.

00:31:59.880 --> 00:32:02.210
They have breached our defensive perimeter
and are coming in at high speed, low altitude.

00:32:06.950 --> 00:32:10.590
Not bad... It's those guys from the
Foreign Legion, right?

00:32:10.590 --> 00:32:12.560
Well, we're going to massacre them!

00:32:14.360 --> 00:32:16.430
Distance at 10... 5...

00:32:16.430 --> 00:32:18.260
Now! Show them our fangs!

00:32:47.660 --> 00:32:48.830
Two enemy craft have made it through!

00:32:48.830 --> 00:32:50.860
They have broken through the last
defensive perimeter!

00:32:50.860 --> 00:32:51.990
What?!

00:33:30.500 --> 00:33:31.670
We did it!

00:33:31.670 --> 00:33:32.940
Shin...

00:33:32.940 --> 00:33:35.280
Drawing in your wing flaps to pass
through those iron fangs

00:33:35.280 --> 00:33:36.610
was just the genius I'd expect of you.

00:33:36.610 --> 00:33:38.370
The same goes for you, Boris.

00:33:38.710 --> 00:33:40.510
It's a good thing we tested to see

00:33:40.510 --> 00:33:44.610
if the rumors that you can fly an F-8
with your wing flaps up were true.

00:33:52.630 --> 00:33:55.300
Mickey! Were you watching out
for us from above?

00:33:55.300 --> 00:33:57.600
I let you guys take care of the big targets,

00:33:57.600 --> 00:33:59.770
while I knocked out anything up at high altitude.

00:33:59.770 --> 00:34:01.030
I see...

00:34:01.030 --> 00:34:04.070
So that's why we weren't attacked from above,

00:34:04.070 --> 00:34:07.170
even though we'd folded our wings
and wobbled through the air.

00:34:07.170 --> 00:34:08.810
You got it.

00:34:08.810 --> 00:34:12.480
Which means we'll have to split the $20,000
reward money three ways.

00:34:12.480 --> 00:34:16.380
No, I think the money will be split only two ways.

00:34:16.380 --> 00:34:17.480
What?

00:34:17.480 --> 00:34:21.480
Boris! If it hadn't been for Mickey's help,
we wouldn't be here right now!

00:34:22.460 --> 00:34:23.560
Boris!

00:34:23.560 --> 00:34:27.790
It's all right, Shin. That's just
the kind of guy he is.

00:34:27.790 --> 00:34:30.960
I don't need that kinda chump change anyhow!

00:34:31.300 --> 00:34:33.200
If that's how it is, then I don't want
my part of it either.

00:34:33.200 --> 00:34:35.830
You can have it all to yourself, Boris.

00:34:40.110 --> 00:34:43.010
You morons are jumping to conclusions!

00:34:43.010 --> 00:34:45.270
When I said it'd be split only two ways...

00:34:47.750 --> 00:34:50.750
I meant for the two of you to split it
between yourselves.

00:34:50.750 --> 00:34:52.420
Boris...

00:34:52.420 --> 00:34:58.330
It looks like I somehow managed to take two or
three shots right through my air intake.

00:35:03.930 --> 00:35:06.570
Friends really are a great thing,

00:35:06.570 --> 00:35:09.640
especially the ones who face death with you.

00:35:09.640 --> 00:35:12.770
You don't run across many people
like that in life.

00:35:12.770 --> 00:35:17.610
But even with friends like that, one or
the other of you is going to die first.

00:35:17.610 --> 00:35:19.640
That's what war is like.

00:35:19.780 --> 00:35:22.050
Heartrending, isn't it?

00:35:22.050 --> 00:35:25.420
That's why I didn't want to make
friends with anyone.

00:35:25.420 --> 00:35:27.450
See, if I put out the lights and go to sleep,

00:35:27.450 --> 00:35:31.120
all the guys who went before me appear.

00:35:34.290 --> 00:35:37.000
First one, then another...

00:35:37.000 --> 00:35:39.360
They say, "Hey, Boris, you doin' all right?"

00:35:44.570 --> 00:35:46.210
Now I'm going too, guys.

00:35:46.210 --> 00:35:48.470
Looks like I'll be able to have a nice,
restful sleep.

00:35:48.810 --> 00:35:50.800
Boris! Pull up!

00:35:55.250 --> 00:36:00.080
Shin, turn out the lights in my room
for me when you get back.

00:36:00.290 --> 00:36:01.720
Boris!

00:36:14.470 --> 00:36:15.740
Well done.

00:36:15.740 --> 00:36:17.770
Since you destroyed that base,

00:36:17.770 --> 00:36:20.510
the supply lines to our enemy's frontline
forces have been cut,

00:36:20.510 --> 00:36:22.670
and it looks as though they have withdrawn.

00:36:23.740 --> 00:36:28.680
So of the twelve planes that sortied out,
only two have returned?

00:36:28.680 --> 00:36:31.550
See that you're well rested before
the next mission.

00:36:32.220 --> 00:36:35.390
Sheesh! That guy's one callous sonnuva bitch!

00:36:35.390 --> 00:36:39.420
And after so many people died on that mission!

00:36:48.600 --> 00:36:50.370
Is this all Boris left behind?

00:36:50.370 --> 00:36:53.170
Yes, Sir. But there's no one to
forward these things on to.

00:36:53.170 --> 00:36:56.200
Although Headquarters will hold on
to them just in case.

00:36:59.280 --> 00:37:00.540
Cut it out!

00:37:10.860 --> 00:37:12.990
Goodnight, Boris.

00:37:39.750 --> 00:37:42.220
Shin, about earlier, I just...

00:37:42.220 --> 00:37:43.920
It's all right.

00:37:47.160 --> 00:37:48.660
It's Bucksey.

00:37:48.660 --> 00:37:52.430
He stands there like that, waiting for his friends
who went out on the last sortie to come back.

00:37:56.070 --> 00:37:58.670
Even though he should know
they're never coming back.

00:37:58.670 --> 00:38:03.610
Those men who died, I wonder what
kinds of lives they lived?

00:38:04.540 --> 00:38:07.350
There are all kinds at this base,

00:38:07.350 --> 00:38:12.590
ex-military, clergymen, boxers,
even Mafia bigwigs.

00:38:12.590 --> 00:38:14.520
They don't talk about it,

00:38:14.520 --> 00:38:17.550
but I'm sure they all have weighty, complicated
reasons for ending up here.

00:38:18.190 --> 00:38:20.390
What about you, Shin?

00:38:27.530 --> 00:38:31.200
I wonder if it's also hot in Tokyo right now?

00:38:40.850 --> 00:38:43.150
Mr. Director, your daughter has arrived.

00:38:43.150 --> 00:38:45.120
Oh, she's here is she?

00:38:46.520 --> 00:38:48.990
Ah, Ryoko, sorry to have you come
all the way here.

00:38:48.990 --> 00:38:50.620
You said there was some business
you wished to see me about.

00:38:50.620 --> 00:38:51.990
What's the matter, Father?

00:38:51.990 --> 00:38:55.050
Ah, well I wouldn't exactly call it "business."

00:38:58.130 --> 00:38:59.500
Have a seat.

00:39:02.840 --> 00:39:04.770
I'm getting on in years myself,

00:39:04.770 --> 00:39:08.770
and I feel bad for always making you
help me out with my own work.

00:39:09.310 --> 00:39:11.280
Oh, don't be silly.

00:39:13.780 --> 00:39:16.280
This is about you getting married.

00:39:16.280 --> 00:39:17.650
Married?

00:39:17.650 --> 00:39:20.250
I thought maybe it was about time.

00:39:20.250 --> 00:39:24.060
Yes, but you see I enjoy the job I have right now,

00:39:24.060 --> 00:39:25.960
and I've just now finally gotten the hang of it.

00:39:25.960 --> 00:39:29.160
I'd like to think I'm of some use
to you here at least!

00:39:29.160 --> 00:39:30.400
And you certainly are!

00:39:30.400 --> 00:39:32.600
I'm not saying this simply because
you're my daughter,

00:39:32.600 --> 00:39:35.340
but your performance is truly commendable.

00:39:35.340 --> 00:39:38.270
In that case, isn't it okay if I go a while
longer not getting married?

00:39:40.040 --> 00:39:43.370
You can't forget about Kazama?

00:39:44.810 --> 00:39:49.580
I understand how you feel, but he
abandoned Yamato Airlines.

00:39:49.580 --> 00:39:53.290
To me, that's tantamount to a dog
biting the hand that feeds it.

00:39:53.290 --> 00:39:54.990
Father!

00:39:54.990 --> 00:39:59.630
Back then I thought either Kazama or Kanzaki
would make a good husband for you.

00:39:59.630 --> 00:40:02.160
They were both the cream of the crop.

00:40:02.160 --> 00:40:04.830
But now that Kazama is no longer here...

00:40:04.830 --> 00:40:07.600
I don't want to hear it!

00:40:14.170 --> 00:40:16.480
You look a little tired.

00:40:16.480 --> 00:40:18.010
He brought up marriage.

00:40:18.010 --> 00:40:20.850
It's so much trouble to refuse.

00:40:20.850 --> 00:40:23.940
He's only doing it because he
cares about you, Miss.

00:40:24.780 --> 00:40:29.880
Ms. Yasuda, do you think that a woman can
live her life with only her memories?

00:40:32.290 --> 00:40:36.700
Memories get romanticized as time moves on.

00:40:36.700 --> 00:40:38.730
You may be right, but still...

00:40:38.730 --> 00:40:41.630
It's possible to live clinging to the past,

00:40:41.630 --> 00:40:44.700
but sometimes you end up missing out on the
happiness that's in front of you right now.

00:40:46.070 --> 00:40:47.710
However...

00:40:47.710 --> 00:40:50.410
If you truly do believe in Mr. Kazama,

00:40:50.410 --> 00:40:52.710
then live on faithfully with that belief.

00:40:52.710 --> 00:40:54.870
I'll always be on your side!

00:40:56.650 --> 00:40:58.020
Thank you.

00:41:02.320 --> 00:41:05.160
For its long-distance direct flights,

00:41:05.160 --> 00:41:08.830
it's only natural that Yamato Airlines would
decide on Maxwell's Type MB-14.

00:41:08.830 --> 00:41:12.370
Provided all Yamato's active pilots
get together and recommend it.

00:41:12.370 --> 00:41:15.130
This is that formal recommendation.

00:41:19.440 --> 00:41:20.740
It certainly is.

00:41:21.570 --> 00:41:24.040
Even I have enough influence
to get a thing like this done.

00:41:24.040 --> 00:41:26.510
There's a hundred thousand shares
in Yamato Airlines

00:41:26.510 --> 00:41:29.450
which I purchased for you
under a different name.

00:41:29.450 --> 00:41:31.990
I'll put it in the safe-deposit box.

00:41:31.990 --> 00:41:33.420
I appreciate it.

00:41:33.420 --> 00:41:38.860
Now you in actuality hold a twenty-five percent
share in Yamato Airlines.

00:41:38.860 --> 00:41:39.960
Yes...

00:41:39.960 --> 00:41:42.400
You're buying up so much stock.

00:41:42.400 --> 00:41:44.760
So are you planning a takeover?

00:41:44.760 --> 00:41:47.600
This is for our mutual profit.

00:41:49.770 --> 00:41:52.440
You certainly are a formidable man.

00:41:52.440 --> 00:41:56.840
Yamato Airlines have no idea what a dreadful foe
they harbor within their own organization.

00:41:59.050 --> 00:42:01.880
Hey, Pops, would you mount some
Sidewinders to my pylons?

00:42:01.880 --> 00:42:03.380
Yeah, sure thing.

00:42:03.380 --> 00:42:05.390
Oh, by the way, Mickey! Have you heard?

00:42:05.390 --> 00:42:06.250
Heard what?

00:42:06.250 --> 00:42:10.490
I hear Shin only has another $20,000 to go
before he's earned the full $1.5 million.

00:42:10.490 --> 00:42:11.820
Really?

00:42:11.820 --> 00:42:13.830
You mean to tell me he's earned that much?

00:42:13.830 --> 00:42:18.460
I figure if he shoots down another
five planes, that should do it.

00:42:18.460 --> 00:42:21.100
So he needs to kill another five people.

00:42:21.100 --> 00:42:24.000
I see... So he'll finally be able to
get outta here, will he?

00:42:24.000 --> 00:42:27.630
That is, if he can make it out alive, of course!

00:42:29.840 --> 00:42:32.440
I'll tell ya, Pops, you really are goin' to Hell.

00:42:39.590 --> 00:42:42.220
One more... Only one more...

00:42:42.220 --> 00:42:44.620
Only one more to go and I'll
have my $1.5 million!

00:42:47.490 --> 00:42:50.630
Ryoko, I'm coming home.

00:42:50.630 --> 00:42:52.100
I can come home!

00:43:06.710 --> 00:43:09.340
Don't think badly of me. You're my last one.

00:43:09.520 --> 00:43:11.680
I won't ever kill again!

00:43:11.680 --> 00:43:14.950
So please... Please forgive me!

00:43:19.130 --> 00:43:20.530
I'm out of ammo!

00:44:01.870 --> 00:44:04.440
That's Shin's Crusader!

00:44:04.440 --> 00:44:05.670
Damn!

00:44:27.090 --> 00:44:28.290
Shin!

00:44:47.110 --> 00:44:48.840
I made it.

00:44:55.390 --> 00:44:58.520
Pops, how much will repairs for this run?

00:44:58.520 --> 00:45:01.660
I hate to say it, but you'd be better off
buying a new plane.

00:45:01.660 --> 00:45:06.160
A comparable plane will probably run you
half a million dollars at least.

00:45:06.970 --> 00:45:11.730
So then earning $20,000 has cost me $500,000?

00:45:12.070 --> 00:45:13.510
Don't let it get to you.

00:45:13.510 --> 00:45:16.480
Just the fact that you made it out of this alive
is enough of a bargain.

00:45:16.480 --> 00:45:21.540
How many more lives do you think I'll have
to take to earn another half million?!

00:45:30.460 --> 00:45:35.120
Mr. Kazama, this thing will protect your life.

00:45:35.560 --> 00:45:37.000
Mind your own business!

00:45:37.000 --> 00:45:40.960
Worry more about your own damn life!

00:45:47.040 --> 00:45:49.570
That guy's got no luck.

00:45:59.250 --> 00:46:01.190
Those three guys...

00:46:01.190 --> 00:46:02.680
Could it be?

00:46:06.360 --> 00:46:08.260
I'm going home.

00:46:08.360 --> 00:46:10.630
I'm going home to Japan.

00:46:10.630 --> 00:46:13.570
I'm going home to Ryoko.

00:46:13.570 --> 00:46:15.570
I'll desert.

00:46:15.570 --> 00:46:19.530
I've had more than I can take of this place!

00:46:37.460 --> 00:46:39.660
There's no way I'll stay in a place like this.

00:46:39.660 --> 00:46:41.290
I'm deserting!

00:46:48.900 --> 00:46:51.570
I'll need one that can fly to Paris
without refueling.

00:46:51.570 --> 00:46:55.170
As for speed, I'd better take one
that can go mach 2 or greater,

00:46:55.170 --> 00:46:58.010
or I won't be able to get away from any missiles.

00:47:00.850 --> 00:47:04.280
Going for a walk so late at night, Mr. Kazama?

00:47:04.280 --> 00:47:07.050
Or were you planning on deserting?

00:47:07.490 --> 00:47:09.890
I know about your circumstances, more or less.

00:47:09.890 --> 00:47:11.860
But this doesn't mean you can desert.

00:47:11.860 --> 00:47:14.990
For one thing, there's no way you'll get away.

00:47:14.990 --> 00:47:19.430
No one in the Middle East has ever
broken away from us.

00:47:19.430 --> 00:47:21.230
You still wanna try your luck against us?

00:47:21.230 --> 00:47:23.260
You guys are...

00:47:23.370 --> 00:47:25.300
The Escape Killers.

00:47:27.540 --> 00:47:28.870
Mickey!

00:47:28.870 --> 00:47:30.980
I finally remembered.

00:47:30.980 --> 00:47:36.440
I recalled hearing a rumor about a trio of guys
who go around finding and killing deserters.

00:47:37.050 --> 00:47:39.450
So who hired you to come to this base?

00:47:39.450 --> 00:47:40.980
Was it Saki?

00:47:42.320 --> 00:47:43.420
Well, no matter.

00:47:43.420 --> 00:47:48.890
You're going up against Shin and me: the
number one and number two men at this base.

00:47:48.890 --> 00:47:53.000
That means at least two of you will be
going to meet your maker.

00:47:53.000 --> 00:47:56.540
Nah, fact is, none of 'em will be
getting out of here alive.

00:47:56.540 --> 00:47:58.640
We'll make sure of that.

00:47:58.640 --> 00:48:02.610
Hey, what's the matter, Escape Killers?

00:48:02.610 --> 00:48:06.150
Ya think you can take us on and make
it outta here in one piece?

00:48:06.150 --> 00:48:09.750
You've made up your minds that this man's
a deserter when he hasn't even deserted.

00:48:09.750 --> 00:48:12.550
How 'bout you start bargaining for your lives?!

00:48:12.550 --> 00:48:14.710
That's enough!

00:48:18.020 --> 00:48:19.360
There you go.

00:48:19.360 --> 00:48:26.370
You'll now return to headquarters and report that
there are no deserters at Area 88, won't you?

00:48:26.370 --> 00:48:28.930
Fine, I got it, Sir.

00:48:29.440 --> 00:48:31.600
Let's blow this joint.

00:48:32.770 --> 00:48:35.670
Hey! Why don't we see 'em off
all the way to the border?

00:48:35.670 --> 00:48:37.110
All right!

00:48:40.780 --> 00:48:42.750
Whoa, hold on a second, Saki!

00:48:42.750 --> 00:48:44.720
What kind of dirty tricks are you pullin'?

00:48:44.720 --> 00:48:47.920
I never thought you'd hire a bunch
of bastards like that!

00:48:47.920 --> 00:48:50.160
I guess you don't think much of me either,

00:48:50.160 --> 00:48:53.690
not if you think I'd hire someone
like the Escape Killers.

00:48:53.690 --> 00:48:55.030
What was that?

00:48:55.030 --> 00:48:57.330
Hold on, Mickey!

00:48:57.330 --> 00:48:59.400
Listen to me, Saki.

00:48:59.400 --> 00:49:00.800
The truth is, I...

00:49:00.800 --> 00:49:02.330
Don't say it, Shin!

00:49:02.330 --> 00:49:04.890
I don't want to hear it either.

00:49:06.340 --> 00:49:09.280
What's the big deal? You'll have it
all back in no time, Shin.

00:49:09.280 --> 00:49:13.510
With skills such as yours, returning home to
Japan should not prove too difficult a task.

00:49:13.510 --> 00:49:14.480
Saki...

00:49:14.480 --> 00:49:17.250
You're fighting so that you can
go home to Japan.

00:49:17.250 --> 00:49:20.780
But what is my reason?

00:49:21.090 --> 00:49:23.690
There is no sadder reality than
that of fellow countrymen

00:49:23.690 --> 00:49:26.330
who spill each others' blood
during a time of civil war.

00:49:26.330 --> 00:49:30.400
My opponent, the leader of the
anti-government faction,

00:49:30.400 --> 00:49:32.630
is my father.

00:49:38.600 --> 00:49:41.710
Shin, do you really want to return
to Japan that badly?

00:49:41.710 --> 00:49:43.480
What about you, Mickey?

00:49:43.480 --> 00:49:46.310
What could have made you want to
come to this godforsaken place?

00:49:46.310 --> 00:49:47.780
Me?

00:49:47.780 --> 00:49:49.220
Good question.

00:49:49.220 --> 00:49:53.090
There was a time when I was like you;
I really, really wanted to go home to New York,

00:49:53.090 --> 00:49:54.550
back when I was in Vietnam.

00:49:55.250 --> 00:49:57.660
That place was Hell.

00:50:25.120 --> 00:50:26.620
"I want to go home."

00:50:26.620 --> 00:50:29.050
"I want to make it back alive, and
walk on home soil once again."

00:50:29.050 --> 00:50:31.590
I remember those were my only thoughts.

00:50:31.590 --> 00:50:33.090
But the thing is...

00:50:33.090 --> 00:50:35.660
When I finally did make it back safe and sound,

00:50:35.660 --> 00:50:38.230
something was different.

00:50:38.230 --> 00:50:39.470
Well...

00:50:39.470 --> 00:50:44.340
My old man, my big brother and my girlfriend,
Tracy, they all treated me real well.

00:50:44.770 --> 00:50:48.840
But there was something in me
that was rejecting them.

00:50:48.840 --> 00:50:50.740
Something...

00:50:51.540 --> 00:50:56.880
I guess as a man who'd been at war for so long,
who'd ridden the fine line between life and death,

00:50:56.880 --> 00:51:00.550
the peaceful life just didn't
agree with me anymore.

00:51:00.550 --> 00:51:03.680
I'll be damned if it doesn't go
beyond all reason though.

00:51:03.920 --> 00:51:06.860
We're two top-notch killers.

00:51:06.860 --> 00:51:11.160
If the scent of blood and gunsmoke that
clings to my body is proof of that,

00:51:11.160 --> 00:51:14.630
then it was a total mistake to think
that such a sonuvabitch killer

00:51:14.630 --> 00:51:18.090
would be able to live among civilians
who don't know anything.

00:51:19.510 --> 00:51:24.380
I don't know what emotional ties
you might have to Japan, to Tokyo,

00:51:24.380 --> 00:51:28.580
but the fact is that you're one
top-notch killer, Shin.

00:51:29.110 --> 00:51:30.080
G'night!

00:51:30.080 --> 00:51:32.480
It'll be a while yet before dawn.

00:51:32.480 --> 00:51:35.780
If you don't get a good rest, it'll be
all the harder from here on.

00:51:41.890 --> 00:51:44.390
A top-notch killer...

00:51:45.730 --> 00:51:48.270
I know that well enough without
him reminding me.

00:51:48.270 --> 00:51:50.960
That's why I want to get out of here!

00:51:55.240 --> 00:51:56.040
Listen up!

00:51:56.040 --> 00:51:58.910
Put the camera against your headrest,
or your photos will be blurred!

00:51:58.910 --> 00:52:01.280
Right! Like this?

00:52:01.280 --> 00:52:03.920
Man, you're a curious one.

00:52:03.920 --> 00:52:07.550
There's no reason you have to come up
in a fighter plane, is there?

00:52:07.550 --> 00:52:12.090
You'll either take some amazing pictures or
you'll lose your life. One or the other, man!

00:52:12.090 --> 00:52:14.150
No kidding.

00:52:14.290 --> 00:52:19.260
But in order to get a peek inside that
guy's mind, I have to do this.

00:52:19.260 --> 00:52:23.640
What is it that calls him to the skies?
What makes him kill other people?

00:52:23.640 --> 00:52:26.140
To find out, I have no choice
but to try flying myself.

00:52:26.140 --> 00:52:28.240
That's the way I see it.

00:52:28.240 --> 00:52:32.540
Shin Kazama, you rank at the top of
all the things that I've covered.

00:52:35.850 --> 00:52:37.620
Ah, here they come.

00:52:37.620 --> 00:52:39.920
Bucksey! You make sure to protect that reporter!

00:52:39.920 --> 00:52:42.080
After all, he paid us a lot of money for this!

00:52:45.520 --> 00:52:48.460
Now don't you go passing out on me, all right?!

00:53:03.310 --> 00:53:05.870
The F-5E Tiger Il, huh?

00:53:07.480 --> 00:53:10.750
I'm impressed you could get
one of these, McCoy.

00:53:11.980 --> 00:53:15.610
As long as you put up the money,
I'll bring you whatever you want!

00:53:15.820 --> 00:53:18.320
Nothing like a brand new plane.

00:53:18.320 --> 00:53:22.060
Why don't we get a picture of it for posterity,
before it gets all beaten up?

00:53:23.360 --> 00:53:24.600
Where's Rocky?

00:53:24.600 --> 00:53:27.670
He's getting a ride in Bucksey's Phantom.

00:53:27.670 --> 00:53:29.300
Bucksey's?

00:53:29.300 --> 00:53:31.940
I hear he asked for the ride and put up
some good money for it.

00:53:31.940 --> 00:53:34.570
'Ole Bucksey was just about jumping for joy.

00:53:34.570 --> 00:53:37.940
I wonder if they'll be all right? That's a total
novice he's taking up there with him.

00:53:37.940 --> 00:53:41.750
Mickey went along as escort.
I don't see any need to worry.

00:53:41.750 --> 00:53:43.580
Mickey did?

00:53:43.580 --> 00:53:45.020
Well, in that case...

00:54:00.330 --> 00:54:02.230
Now this is how you dogfight!

00:54:02.230 --> 00:54:04.700
I'll bet you're getting some
pretty wild pictures, huh?

00:54:33.230 --> 00:54:36.030
Bucksey! Missiles on your six!

00:54:45.380 --> 00:54:47.650
Bucksey! We don't have time to
turn around and escape.

00:54:47.650 --> 00:54:49.620
Stall 'em out and shake 'em off that way!

00:55:08.900 --> 00:55:10.930
What's going on?!

00:55:12.540 --> 00:55:14.410
Redout!

00:55:14.410 --> 00:55:15.870
As a result of excessive negative
Gs on your body,

00:55:15.870 --> 00:55:20.070
the blood vessels in your eyes are overloaded,
and everything looks red!

00:55:24.050 --> 00:55:26.250
If you keep it up for too long,
you'll lose your eyesight.

00:55:26.250 --> 00:55:29.720
It can cause a brain hemorrhage too,
but try to bear it a bit longer!

00:55:29.720 --> 00:55:31.160
Just hang in there!

00:55:33.990 --> 00:55:36.020
Okay, we're gonna lose it!

00:55:44.140 --> 00:55:45.300
Bucksey!

00:55:47.240 --> 00:55:50.340
It looks okay. You'll be able to rake
in the cash with this plane.

00:55:50.340 --> 00:55:52.810
Fly this one more patiently, all right?

00:55:56.820 --> 00:55:59.380
Looks like Mickey's back.

00:55:59.850 --> 00:56:02.190
I'm surprised you can make out his plane
through the heat haze.

00:56:02.190 --> 00:56:04.660
It's the sound, the sound.

00:56:04.660 --> 00:56:09.260
His fuel pump isn't a genuine
North American pump.

00:56:09.260 --> 00:56:14.600
What he's got on there now is some random one
that fell off an enemy plane a while back.

00:56:14.600 --> 00:56:16.400
That's insane!

00:56:16.400 --> 00:56:19.170
What's the big deal? As long as
he's got a cap on it, it's fine.

00:56:19.170 --> 00:56:21.540
That's how machines work.

00:56:21.540 --> 00:56:24.670
Don't tell me this Tiger Il is also like that.

00:56:25.140 --> 00:56:27.040
This one's all right.

00:56:31.150 --> 00:56:35.050
Bucksey's Phantom isn't with him, is it?

00:56:37.590 --> 00:56:38.680
Rocky...

00:57:01.180 --> 00:57:01.480
Yamato
Airlines
Reception

00:57:01.480 --> 00:57:03.350
Thank you so much for your invitation.

00:57:03.350 --> 00:57:07.320
We are truly in your debt, Sir.
Please, come in and enjoy yourselves.

00:57:10.720 --> 00:57:12.590
Ah, welcome.

00:57:12.590 --> 00:57:16.090
Tonight you look even more radiant
than usual, my dear.

00:57:16.090 --> 00:57:18.200
Oh my! Thank you very much.

00:57:18.200 --> 00:57:24.140
YAMATO AIRLINES
30TH ANNIVERSARY PARTY

00:57:25.640 --> 00:57:27.300
Please enjoy yourselves.

00:57:27.540 --> 00:57:29.440
Do you have a moment, Ryoko?

00:57:29.440 --> 00:57:31.210
Ah, Mr. Kanzaki. Right now, I'm a little...

00:57:31.210 --> 00:57:32.440
Ryoko...

00:57:32.440 --> 00:57:33.500
Come on.

00:57:35.410 --> 00:57:37.380
What exactly do you want?

00:57:37.380 --> 00:57:40.290
I trust the company president
has spoken with you?

00:57:40.290 --> 00:57:41.990
About what?

00:57:41.990 --> 00:57:46.120
About how I asked him for
your hand in marriage!

00:57:46.120 --> 00:57:48.590
If you haven't spoken to him, then
maybe now is a good time to...

00:57:48.590 --> 00:57:50.400
I don't think so!

00:57:50.400 --> 00:57:51.600
I've always...

00:57:51.600 --> 00:57:54.900
I believe you are aware of how I feel.

00:57:54.900 --> 00:57:57.170
Kazama isn't here anymore!

00:57:57.170 --> 00:57:59.500
I wish he had never stolen you from me!

00:57:59.500 --> 00:58:01.110
Now that he's gone...

00:58:01.110 --> 00:58:03.940
It's a big relief for you, right?

00:58:05.080 --> 00:58:07.210
I was wrong about you.

00:58:13.990 --> 00:58:15.650
Miss Tsugumo!

00:58:15.650 --> 00:58:17.620
I'm sick of it all!

00:58:17.620 --> 00:58:19.390
Please sit down and have a little rest.

00:58:19.390 --> 00:58:21.050
I'll go make some tea.

00:58:51.720 --> 00:58:53.090
This is...

00:58:53.090 --> 00:58:54.920
Is something wrong?

00:58:57.900 --> 00:59:00.930
Look at this! Shin! It's Shin!

00:59:00.930 --> 00:59:02.370
What?

00:59:02.500 --> 00:59:04.640
Where?

00:59:04.640 --> 00:59:06.000
Right here.

00:59:06.000 --> 00:59:07.630
Here!

00:59:10.140 --> 00:59:13.550
It's so small I can't really tell for sure,

00:59:13.550 --> 00:59:14.610
but now that you mention it...

00:59:14.610 --> 00:59:16.210
Shin's alive!

00:59:16.210 --> 00:59:18.380
He was alive all along!

00:59:18.380 --> 00:59:20.020
"Photo by Rocky."

00:59:20.020 --> 00:59:21.990
That's the person who took these pictures!

00:59:21.990 --> 00:59:24.620
The publisher is "World Press."

00:59:24.620 --> 00:59:26.320
I'm going to call them.

00:59:26.320 --> 00:59:28.920
Please take care of things for me
in the assembly hall.

00:59:33.200 --> 00:59:34.890
Miss Tsugumo!

00:59:35.730 --> 00:59:37.870
Is something the matter, Ms. Yasuda?

00:59:37.870 --> 00:59:40.100
Uh, no, it's nothing.

00:59:57.120 --> 00:59:58.820
Shin!

00:59:59.160 --> 01:00:02.030
So he's still alive?!

01:00:10.370 --> 01:00:12.040
Miss Tsugumo?

01:00:12.040 --> 01:00:14.410
They said that man named Rocky

01:00:14.410 --> 01:00:16.740
died while covering that story.

01:00:16.740 --> 01:00:18.540
Oh, dear...

01:00:20.110 --> 01:00:22.550
My only lead has vanished.

01:00:25.780 --> 01:00:28.520
It's all right, Miss Tsugumo!

01:00:28.520 --> 01:00:31.690
There were military planes in that photograph.

01:00:31.690 --> 01:00:34.760
I know someone who is a military analyst.

01:00:34.760 --> 01:00:37.730
Why don't we bring him that picture
tomorrow morning? Okay?

01:00:42.030 --> 01:00:45.700
This is a picture from the Aslan civil war front.

01:00:45.700 --> 01:00:50.110
Furthermore, the planes are equipped in a rather
haphazard fashion and bear no rank insignia.

01:00:50.110 --> 01:00:52.180
It may be a foreign legion.

01:00:52.180 --> 01:00:54.050
A foreign legion?

01:00:54.050 --> 01:00:57.150
Such legions are often formed in
the Middle East and in Africa

01:00:57.150 --> 01:01:00.490
when war breaks out in impoverished countries.

01:01:00.490 --> 01:01:02.520
How can they afford that,
if they're impoverished?

01:01:02.520 --> 01:01:07.260
It takes a lot of time and money for an amateur
to become a decent soldier.

01:01:07.260 --> 01:01:09.830
One fighter plane costs around three billion yen.

01:01:09.830 --> 01:01:14.370
However, it costs several times more to
train the pilot who will fly that plane.

01:01:14.370 --> 01:01:15.430
That much?

01:01:15.430 --> 01:01:19.960
So it's much more affordable to
hire professional soldiers.

01:01:20.570 --> 01:01:22.540
Then Shin is also...

01:01:22.540 --> 01:01:25.310
In one instance several years ago, a Japanese
student who was studying abroad

01:01:25.310 --> 01:01:27.650
signed an official document without
understanding what it was

01:01:27.650 --> 01:01:31.110
and was taken off to the foreign
legion straight away.

01:01:33.320 --> 01:01:35.390
Outside of Japan,

01:01:35.390 --> 01:01:38.790
an individual's signature holds the same validity
that family seal stamps do here.

01:01:39.690 --> 01:01:45.360
Aslan's foreign legion encompasses
Areas 81 through 88.

01:01:45.800 --> 01:01:50.390
Perhaps this Kazama is at Area 88.

01:01:52.970 --> 01:01:56.540
Areas 82 and 83 merged to form Area 84,

01:01:56.540 --> 01:01:59.710
and were then incorporated into the
regular army along with Area 85.

01:01:59.710 --> 01:02:04.850
Areas 86 and 87 provide helicopter
support to the ground forces.

01:02:04.850 --> 01:02:08.820
That leaves Areas 81 and 88,

01:02:08.820 --> 01:02:13.020
but Area 81 is a small base which houses an
assortment of cheap counter-insurgency aircraft.

01:02:13.020 --> 01:02:14.990
Which I suspect means he is at...

01:02:14.990 --> 01:02:16.660
Area 88!

01:02:23.000 --> 01:02:24.570
How do we get there?

01:02:24.570 --> 01:02:26.640
I'm afraid I don't know.

01:02:26.640 --> 01:02:30.510
After all, if they gave out the location, it wouldn't
be much of a military secret then.

01:02:30.510 --> 01:02:31.740
Ms. Yasuda,

01:02:31.740 --> 01:02:34.950
we're scheduled to visit several of our local
branches in France next week, aren't we?

01:02:34.950 --> 01:02:36.720
Yes!

01:02:36.720 --> 01:02:39.820
On the way back I'll take the southern route
and stop in Tel Aviv.

01:02:39.820 --> 01:02:41.490
Please make the necessary arrangements.

01:02:41.490 --> 01:02:43.260
Don't tell me you're planning to...

01:02:43.260 --> 01:02:45.860
Why, Aslan is in the middle of
a civil war right now!

01:02:45.860 --> 01:02:49.790
This must be kept a secret from my father.
I can't have him worrying about me.

01:03:15.450 --> 01:03:17.820
Yes, that's right, Ms. Yasuda!

01:03:23.030 --> 01:03:25.260
Captain Kanzaki, what are you...

01:03:25.260 --> 01:03:27.160
Why?

01:03:27.500 --> 01:03:32.370
I found out that you were going to Tel Aviv,
so I'm here to stop you.

01:03:32.370 --> 01:03:34.070
What did you say?

01:03:34.440 --> 01:03:37.480
There's no need for you to go so far
with your local branch visits

01:03:37.480 --> 01:03:41.310
as to expose yourself to danger visiting
countries experiencing political unrest.

01:03:41.310 --> 01:03:43.750
What right do you have to stop me?

01:03:43.750 --> 01:03:45.350
I'm under orders from the company president.

01:03:45.350 --> 01:03:45.850
What?!

01:03:45.850 --> 01:03:47.250
Captain Kanzaki!
What?!

01:03:47.250 --> 01:03:49.390
You told him about this, didn't you?

01:03:49.390 --> 01:03:51.320
This is for your own good, Miss.

01:03:52.490 --> 01:03:53.990
You'll be coming back on my plane,

01:03:53.990 --> 01:03:56.150
and there won't be any stopping in Tel Aviv.

01:04:16.480 --> 01:04:18.080
Monsieur Kanzaki?

01:04:18.080 --> 01:04:19.480
<i>Yes...</i>

01:04:21.250 --> 01:04:22.880
I <i>f y</i> o <i>u p</i> I <i>ease...</i>

01:05:06.200 --> 01:05:10.500
Welcome, I am Giuseppe Farina.

01:05:10.600 --> 01:05:13.570
I am Kanzaki from Yamato Airlines.

01:05:15.910 --> 01:05:18.410
What would you like to drink?

01:05:18.410 --> 01:05:22.780
We have wine, scotch and
all manner of vintage.

01:05:22.780 --> 01:05:26.050
I'm afraid it's not my policy to drink
before conducting business.

01:05:26.050 --> 01:05:28.420
Well now, you're a very proper man, aren't you?

01:05:28.420 --> 01:05:32.360
And what brings such a proper man here
with an assassination request?

01:05:32.460 --> 01:05:33.860
I have two reasons.

01:05:33.960 --> 01:05:37.300
First, I myself have no training
in the art of killing people,

01:05:37.300 --> 01:05:41.030
and second, because I don't want to
get my own hands dirty.

01:05:41.030 --> 01:05:43.670
Very good. And the target?

01:05:43.670 --> 01:05:46.740
His name is Shin Kazama, Japanese.

01:05:46.740 --> 01:05:51.080
He's at a base called Area 88, which is in Aslan.

01:05:51.080 --> 01:05:53.140
He's the commander of a foreign legion.

01:05:53.410 --> 01:05:55.740
Area 88...

01:05:55.880 --> 01:05:59.850
You're able to rub out anyone, no matter
where in the world they are.

01:05:59.850 --> 01:06:02.990
You can even freely control the Mafia.

01:06:02.990 --> 01:06:05.180
Or so I hear...

01:06:23.010 --> 01:06:24.440
Not very talkative, are you?

01:06:24.440 --> 01:06:27.980
Italian men are much more cheerful
and conversational.

01:06:27.980 --> 01:06:29.880
Or is it something else?

01:06:29.880 --> 01:06:33.650
Perhaps you regret betraying your friend?

01:06:33.650 --> 01:06:36.350
I don't feel any sense of remorse.

01:06:36.350 --> 01:06:39.260
I sold my soul over to the devil long ago.

01:07:07.720 --> 01:07:09.450
Little Leaves Orphanage

01:07:09.450 --> 01:07:11.360
Little Leaves Orphanage
It's snowing!

01:07:11.360 --> 01:07:12.820
Little Leaves Orphanage
It is, it really is!

01:07:12.820 --> 01:07:13.490
It is, it really is!

01:07:13.490 --> 01:07:15.660
Oh my, it is!

01:07:15.660 --> 01:07:18.820
Okay then, everyone, let's go out
and have a snowball fight!

01:07:24.300 --> 01:07:27.370
Hey, c'mon, let's go outside!

01:07:27.370 --> 01:07:27.940
Let's play together.

01:07:27.940 --> 01:07:28.510
That's all right.
Let's play together.

01:07:28.510 --> 01:07:29.270
That's all right.

01:07:29.270 --> 01:07:31.740
My name's Shin Kazama.

01:07:31.740 --> 01:07:34.280
You're that guy, Satoru, who just came
in yesterday, right?

01:07:34.280 --> 01:07:37.050
Yeah, Satoru Kanzaki.

01:07:37.050 --> 01:07:40.690
The director was saying that
you're really tough!

01:07:40.690 --> 01:07:43.620
He says usually kids cry all night long
when they come here.

01:07:43.620 --> 01:07:46.160
But he says you didn't.

01:07:46.160 --> 01:07:48.330
Did you cry?

01:07:48.330 --> 01:07:49.760
Dunno...

01:07:49.760 --> 01:07:54.600
I don't really know, because I was left on the
doorstep of this place when I was real little.

01:07:54.600 --> 01:07:58.660
I was a baby, so I probably screamed
and cried, I guess.

01:07:59.740 --> 01:08:01.270
Hey, tell me something...

01:08:01.270 --> 01:08:03.810
What are mothers like?

01:08:03.810 --> 01:08:06.610
See, I don't know my mother.

01:08:06.610 --> 01:08:09.310
So tell me, okay?

01:08:14.250 --> 01:08:16.350
Well, moms are...

01:08:16.350 --> 01:08:19.990
real warm and soft...

01:08:19.990 --> 01:08:21.730
and they smell nice...

01:08:21.730 --> 01:08:24.660
And? C'mon, tell me, what else?

01:08:24.660 --> 01:08:28.390
And they're really comforting to be with!

01:08:40.240 --> 01:08:47.390
Warm, soft, nice-smelling and comforting...

01:08:47.390 --> 01:08:50.010
And then she tossed me aside!

01:08:50.320 --> 01:08:54.260
I hate my mother for leaving me these memories
of what it's like to have her!

01:08:54.260 --> 01:08:56.460
I hate people!

01:08:56.460 --> 01:08:59.450
I hate anyone who's ahead of me!

01:09:06.200 --> 01:09:08.610
Shin Kazama...

01:09:08.610 --> 01:09:11.010
Even though you and I came from
almost the same background,

01:09:11.010 --> 01:09:13.740
you were always a step ahead of me.

01:09:19.220 --> 01:09:21.550
Not only were you a better pilot,

01:09:21.550 --> 01:09:24.820
but you also got Ryoko, and widened
the gap between you and me!

01:09:30.360 --> 01:09:32.430
You're an eyesore, Shin!

01:09:32.430 --> 01:09:36.330
There is no one in the world who's
more of an eyesore than you!

01:09:38.670 --> 01:09:42.210
"Hey! What are mothers like?"

01:09:42.210 --> 01:09:44.810
"See, I don't know my mother."

01:09:44.810 --> 01:09:47.610
"So tell me, okay?"

01:09:56.020 --> 01:09:57.060
It's Charlie!

01:09:57.060 --> 01:09:59.590
Charlie the Phoenix is back!

01:09:59.590 --> 01:10:01.960
Didn't he call it quits?!

01:10:09.430 --> 01:10:12.700
Has he come to die again?

01:10:12.700 --> 01:10:14.910
Hey, Charlie! Long time, no see, man!

01:10:14.910 --> 01:10:17.110
Heya, Mickey. So you're still alive, huh?

01:10:17.110 --> 01:10:19.310
I bet you felt dead living the civilian life again.

01:10:19.310 --> 01:10:24.280
No kidding, once the smell of gunpowder gets
through to your core, there's no turning back.

01:10:24.280 --> 01:10:26.120
You say that now, but as soon as you put
your life on the line here again,

01:10:26.120 --> 01:10:27.720
you'll be wishing you were back
in that other world, right?

01:10:27.720 --> 01:10:28.890
You got it.

01:10:28.890 --> 01:10:32.860
Whether it's coming here or going back,
either way I choose, I still wind up in Hell!

01:10:32.860 --> 01:10:35.390
Well, you're welcome here.
It's good to have you back.

01:10:35.390 --> 01:10:36.530
Is Saki at the command center?

01:10:36.530 --> 01:10:39.160
Nah, he's off negotiating air transport
routes coming through Paris.

01:10:39.160 --> 01:10:41.220
He'll probably be back today.

01:10:42.530 --> 01:10:45.770
Hey, Shin! Let me introduce you to someone.

01:10:45.770 --> 01:10:47.840
This is Charlie the Phoenix.

01:10:47.840 --> 01:10:51.710
This is Shin Kazama. He's been number one
at Area 88 ever since you left.

01:10:51.710 --> 01:10:54.010
And of course I'm number two.

01:10:58.080 --> 01:11:01.520
Nice to meet you, Shin Kazama.

01:11:04.420 --> 01:11:05.790
It's no use.

01:11:05.790 --> 01:11:09.830
Whatever airline I go to, as soon as I give our
names, they say all their flights are booked.

01:11:09.830 --> 01:11:11.500
I see...

01:11:11.500 --> 01:11:15.000
I'm sure that Captain Kanzaki is behind this.

01:11:15.000 --> 01:11:17.730
I'll go try asking once more.

01:11:19.140 --> 01:11:21.410
Please pardon me, Mademoiselle.

01:11:21.410 --> 01:11:23.210
Not at all, it was my fault.

01:11:23.210 --> 01:11:25.440
Excuse me.

01:11:40.790 --> 01:11:43.390
Cheer up, Miss Tsugumo.

01:11:45.160 --> 01:11:47.460
Pardon me.

01:11:50.770 --> 01:11:53.260
So you're also on this flight?

01:11:54.070 --> 01:11:57.140
I'm on my way to Tokyo. And you?

01:11:57.140 --> 01:11:59.940
I'm changing flights in Tel Aviv,
en route to Aslan.

01:11:59.940 --> 01:12:01.740
Aslan?!

01:12:24.970 --> 01:12:27.740
We're now at an altitude of 30,000 feet.

01:12:27.740 --> 01:12:30.570
All right, I'll switch to autopilot.

01:12:34.610 --> 01:12:37.620
Ryoko, I'm not letting you off in Tel Aviv.

01:12:37.620 --> 01:12:40.240
Not that you'd be able to see Kazama
even if you did get off!

01:12:43.220 --> 01:12:46.020
Captain, we're receiving a call from
Paris Flight Control.

01:12:46.020 --> 01:12:47.860
What could it be?

01:12:48.660 --> 01:12:53.030
This is Yamato Airlines, Flight 82,
Captain Kanzaki speaking.

01:12:54.300 --> 01:12:55.130
What was that?!

01:12:55.130 --> 01:12:56.570
What is it, Sir?

01:12:56.570 --> 01:12:59.870
Somebody's set bombs on this plane.

01:12:59.870 --> 01:13:01.640
Where is it?

01:13:01.940 --> 01:13:03.410
What?

01:13:08.950 --> 01:13:10.820
Who did it, Captain?

01:13:10.820 --> 01:13:13.180
They said he's been caught by the Paris police.

01:13:13.180 --> 01:13:15.620
Let's turn around immediately, and
get the passengers to safety!

01:13:15.620 --> 01:13:16.890
Out of the question.

01:13:16.890 --> 01:13:18.360
But why, Sir?

01:13:18.360 --> 01:13:20.690
If we reduce our altitude, it'll go off.

01:13:20.690 --> 01:13:23.320
Apparently, it's linked to our pressure altimeter.

01:13:23.760 --> 01:13:25.960
There are two, on the left and right wing joints,

01:13:25.960 --> 01:13:28.690
with more than enough explosives
to blow this plane to bits!

01:13:33.970 --> 01:13:37.140
When we reached an altitude of 5000 meters,
the bombs were armed,

01:13:37.140 --> 01:13:39.940
and then at 10,000 meters, a time-activated
switch was also armed.

01:13:43.650 --> 01:13:46.320
At this rate, in three hours we'll all
be blown to smithereens.

01:13:46.320 --> 01:13:47.890
What are the bomber's demands?

01:13:47.890 --> 01:13:50.120
The life of a certain individual onboard.

01:13:50.120 --> 01:13:54.390
In other words, this is not a hijacking,
but an assassination plot!

01:13:57.300 --> 01:13:59.160
Mr. Saki Vashtar, I presume?

01:13:59.160 --> 01:14:00.600
I am.

01:14:00.600 --> 01:14:03.800
I'm terribly sorry, but would you please
move over there to the lounge?

01:14:03.900 --> 01:14:05.300
Me?

01:14:07.040 --> 01:14:08.610
What? Explosives?!

01:14:08.610 --> 01:14:09.440
That's right.

01:14:09.440 --> 01:14:10.910
Because of you, one individual,

01:14:10.910 --> 01:14:14.000
three hundred passengers will be blown away
along with this plane!

01:14:15.380 --> 01:14:19.420
Hey! Don't you have anything to say?
Who the hell are you anyway?

01:14:19.420 --> 01:14:21.390
Who's trying to kill you?

01:14:21.390 --> 01:14:23.750
There are many who wish me dead.

01:14:23.750 --> 01:14:26.860
I hold the rank of lieutenant colonel
in the Aslan Royal Air Force.

01:14:26.860 --> 01:14:29.990
I am also commanding officer
of our foreign legion,

01:14:29.990 --> 01:14:31.900
which has been the scourge of the rebel forces.

01:14:32.230 --> 01:14:33.630
Foreign legion?!

01:14:33.630 --> 01:14:35.870
What was that?! Yamato Airlines?

01:14:35.870 --> 01:14:39.130
Correct, a Japanese plane.

01:14:40.740 --> 01:14:43.110
And what type of explosives are being used?

01:14:43.110 --> 01:14:45.680
Our aircraft passed the weight check,

01:14:45.680 --> 01:14:47.380
so I believe they are using plastic explosives.

01:14:47.380 --> 01:14:48.900
Son of a bitch!

01:14:55.750 --> 01:14:58.020
They will detonate in two hours.

01:14:58.020 --> 01:14:59.320
Two hours?!

01:14:59.320 --> 01:15:00.660
We cannot reduce our altitude.

01:15:00.660 --> 01:15:04.900
The fates of three hundred lives
are now in your hands.

01:15:04.900 --> 01:15:06.530
Hold on a minute, Saki.

01:15:06.530 --> 01:15:09.730
Whether I'm flying in close to another aircraft
or sneaking under its wings,

01:15:09.730 --> 01:15:11.800
either way, if I take my Tiger Il...

01:15:11.800 --> 01:15:13.440
Use my Kfir.

01:15:13.440 --> 01:15:14.840
The Kfir has a delta wing design.

01:15:14.840 --> 01:15:18.580
Plus, it has canards located on
the sides of its air intakes.

01:15:18.580 --> 01:15:21.080
In terms of stability, it surpasses
all other delta designs.

01:15:21.080 --> 01:15:24.320
What's more, its onboard machine guns
can fire single rounds.

01:15:24.320 --> 01:15:26.250
They're DEFA 30mm cannons.

01:15:26.250 --> 01:15:28.820
Even so, your altitude is 10,000 meters!

01:15:28.820 --> 01:15:31.390
If we screw this up, it's the end of
everyone on board.

01:15:31.390 --> 01:15:33.090
Why did you choose us?

01:15:33.090 --> 01:15:36.960
Someone who is skilled at killing should
also know how to save lives.

01:15:36.960 --> 01:15:41.100
You aren't called the number one and
number two men of Area 88 for nothing.

01:15:41.100 --> 01:15:43.830
Area 88?!

01:15:44.070 --> 01:15:48.740
The contact point is RL-22C.
Be up here in thirty minutes.

01:15:48.740 --> 01:15:51.280
Shin... Mickey... I'm counting on you!

01:15:51.280 --> 01:15:52.870
Shin?!

01:16:09.830 --> 01:16:12.030
That's a Yamato Airlines international flight.

01:16:12.030 --> 01:16:15.300
I guess it's no surprise that I'd come across one,
even in the skies of the Middle East.

01:16:15.300 --> 01:16:16.470
Ryoko...

01:16:16.470 --> 01:16:18.370
What are you doing right now?

01:16:28.080 --> 01:16:29.740
Mickey! That's it!

01:16:44.730 --> 01:16:47.250
Saki, we've confirmed the location
of the explosives!

01:16:59.610 --> 01:17:03.650
It's no good. The engine pods are in the way,
so firing at an angle from behind won't work!

01:17:03.650 --> 01:17:05.740
Then let's approach from the front.

01:17:10.190 --> 01:17:11.390
No good.

01:17:11.390 --> 01:17:13.460
It's a small target already, and
we're going too fast.

01:17:13.460 --> 01:17:15.690
It's way too hard to get a reliable fix on it!

01:17:28.110 --> 01:17:29.510
What the hell are we going to do?!

01:17:29.510 --> 01:17:31.010
Even coming in from behind,

01:17:31.010 --> 01:17:34.740
our tail fins are going to keep us from getting
really close to the targets underneath that plane!

01:17:35.180 --> 01:17:37.620
It doesn't matter how good your
subordinates may be,

01:17:37.620 --> 01:17:41.790
it will be impossible to shoot off the bombs
attached to this plane's underside!

01:17:41.790 --> 01:17:44.250
Then I guess you'd rather die like this?

01:17:44.620 --> 01:17:47.490
Shin! We won't accomplish anything
just screwing around like this.

01:17:47.490 --> 01:17:48.660
Why don't I try firing off a round?

01:17:48.660 --> 01:17:49.990
Mickey...

01:17:49.990 --> 01:17:51.400
That's it!

01:17:51.400 --> 01:17:54.260
If we fly inverted, our tail fins
won't be in the way.

01:17:54.530 --> 01:17:56.100
What?!

01:17:56.100 --> 01:17:59.800
You telling me we're going to roll over and skim
along the underbelly of a passenger plane?!

01:18:00.100 --> 01:18:02.610
It's the only way we'll be able to
line up our targets.

01:18:02.610 --> 01:18:05.240
Mickey, you get the right one. I've got the left!

01:18:05.880 --> 01:18:08.210
All right! Let's do it!

01:18:08.650 --> 01:18:11.240
This is Shin. I'm moving in on the target!

01:18:39.540 --> 01:18:40.770
What's going on?!

01:18:41.480 --> 01:18:42.480
Here they come!

01:18:42.480 --> 01:18:44.450
Hold it steady!

01:19:13.280 --> 01:19:14.280
We did it!

01:19:14.280 --> 01:19:16.650
Whew! I thought I was gonna die!

01:19:21.720 --> 01:19:24.710
I'm very impressed. Good job!

01:19:30.660 --> 01:19:32.400
I can't thank you enough.

01:19:32.400 --> 01:19:36.200
It's those two pilots whom you should thank:
Mickey Simon and Shin Kazama.

01:19:45.610 --> 01:19:47.270
Shin...

01:19:52.280 --> 01:19:55.190
Miss Tsugumo, it's a fighter plane.

01:20:00.660 --> 01:20:02.830
What happened just now?

01:20:02.830 --> 01:20:04.420
Did it have something to do
with that fighter plane?

01:20:04.960 --> 01:20:06.230
It's nothing, Miss.

01:20:06.230 --> 01:20:08.200
That is just one of my subordinates.

01:20:39.900 --> 01:20:43.270
Goodbye, Yamato Airlines.

01:21:12.300 --> 01:21:14.570
Papa Wolf to the Wolf Pack.

01:21:14.570 --> 01:21:17.870
Today's objective is a measly,
dirt poor little base.

01:21:17.870 --> 01:21:20.060
Take this mission as you would a training
exercise. Now go have some fun!

01:21:20.800 --> 01:21:21.970
Attack!

01:22:32.040 --> 01:22:34.680
They snuck under the radar and
flew in nap-of-the-earth.

01:22:34.680 --> 01:22:37.380
One squadron established air superiority.

01:22:37.380 --> 01:22:40.120
The remaining three squadrons
centered around the runway

01:22:40.120 --> 01:22:42.590
and attacked the areas to the
left and right of it.

01:22:42.590 --> 01:22:46.820
And then, when the three squadrons completed
their attack and started to turn around,

01:22:46.820 --> 01:22:49.830
the high altitude squadron crushed all
targets that had been omitted,

01:22:49.830 --> 01:22:52.360
and then the entire formation
flew off towards Germany.

01:22:52.360 --> 01:22:56.420
Thus, Area 81 was completely annihilated.

01:22:56.970 --> 01:23:00.960
Saki, that's a tactic I used all the time in Vietnam.

01:23:01.840 --> 01:23:07.440
There aren't any pilots in the rebel army who
could pull off such a precise attack.

01:23:07.440 --> 01:23:09.680
Those guys are pros among pros.

01:23:09.680 --> 01:23:11.720
So are those guys mercs too?

01:23:11.720 --> 01:23:16.020
The rebel army has hired a
foreign legion like ours.

01:23:16.650 --> 01:23:18.850
It's a distinct possibility, Saki.

01:23:22.530 --> 01:23:23.760
Enemy sighted!

01:23:24.830 --> 01:23:26.230
Control Tower to Commander Saki!

01:23:26.230 --> 01:23:28.200
We are under attack from
the southwest quadrant!

01:23:28.200 --> 01:23:29.930
Twelve units sighted!

01:23:30.900 --> 01:23:32.500
They've come to pay us a visit.

01:23:32.500 --> 01:23:35.710
Their primary objective is Area 88!

01:23:35.710 --> 01:23:37.170
It's mercenary versus mercenary.

01:23:37.270 --> 01:23:39.610
We will get in formation and counterattack.

01:23:39.610 --> 01:23:42.310
I will lead the counterattack.

01:23:42.580 --> 01:23:43.580
Interesting...

01:23:43.580 --> 01:23:46.580
Well then, I'll just let the enemy
show me what they can do.

01:23:46.580 --> 01:23:50.490
And while I'm at it, I'll check out the skills
of Area 88's number one pilot too.

01:23:58.930 --> 01:24:00.960
Wolf Pack 3 to Papa Wolf.

01:24:00.960 --> 01:24:03.500
It looks like Area 88 has dispatched its planes.

01:24:03.500 --> 01:24:06.700
They're like us, another foreign legion
flying over the Middle East.

01:24:06.700 --> 01:24:08.600
Give them our warmest welcome.

01:24:30.390 --> 01:24:33.330
I'll share some information on the
enemy foreign legion.

01:24:33.660 --> 01:24:36.300
The aircraft they're using is the MiG-27D.

01:24:36.300 --> 01:24:38.300
They are a team of about fifteen planes.

01:24:38.300 --> 01:24:41.340
They are highly skilled in both air to ground
and air to air maneuvers.

01:24:41.340 --> 01:24:43.270
Their code name is "Wolf Pack,"

01:24:43.270 --> 01:24:46.040
and their commander flies under
the callsign "Papa Wolf."

01:24:46.040 --> 01:24:48.670
The team's usual tactics are unknown.

01:24:56.290 --> 01:24:59.450
Range on! Fan out!

01:27:48.890 --> 01:27:51.630
So you avoided it by using your
afterburners, huh?

01:27:51.630 --> 01:27:53.300
That's Charlie the Phoenix, isn't it?

01:27:53.300 --> 01:27:54.630
What do you think you're doing?!

01:27:54.630 --> 01:27:57.930
I've been given a task: to get rid of you!

01:27:57.930 --> 01:27:59.000
By who?!

01:27:59.000 --> 01:28:00.070
I can't say.

01:28:00.070 --> 01:28:02.470
This is business, see.

01:28:02.910 --> 01:28:04.970
Farewell, Shin Kazama!

01:28:59.860 --> 01:29:02.670
They were difficult opponents,
worthy of their reputation.

01:29:02.670 --> 01:29:05.870
Fifteen aircraft went out on this sortie, and a
full ten of them will not be returning.

01:29:05.870 --> 01:29:09.140
And Charlie and Shin Kazama were
among those casualties.

01:29:09.640 --> 01:29:12.940
Charlie the Phoenix and Shin Kazama, huh?

01:29:12.940 --> 01:29:15.670
I thought those two were invincible.

01:29:40.400 --> 01:29:42.710
I wonder how it turned out?

01:29:42.710 --> 01:29:44.900
It's terribly quiet.

01:29:45.410 --> 01:29:50.010
I wonder if the guys from Area 88
were able to return safely?

01:29:51.780 --> 01:29:54.820
I'm not going to die.

01:29:54.820 --> 01:29:57.150
No way am I dying in a place like this!

01:29:57.750 --> 01:29:59.590
Not before I see Ryoko again!

01:29:59.590 --> 01:30:02.250
And not before I see Kanzaki
and find out the truth!

01:30:14.970 --> 01:30:17.100
I won't return to the Area ever again.

01:30:17.440 --> 01:30:18.910
I'm going back to Japan!

01:30:42.630 --> 01:30:43.630
Damn it...

01:30:43.630 --> 01:30:47.300
I'm not dying in this kind of a place!

01:32:59.070 --> 01:33:00.330
Water...

01:33:00.670 --> 01:33:02.400
Water...

01:33:19.190 --> 01:33:21.850
Am I going to die here?

01:33:24.190 --> 01:33:26.500
It's probably not so bad,

01:33:26.500 --> 01:33:29.860
falling asleep in the embrace of the hot sand.

01:33:55.330 --> 01:33:57.020
Shin!

01:34:04.000 --> 01:34:06.030
Ryoko!

01:34:07.640 --> 01:34:09.870
My heart's still beating.

01:34:10.410 --> 01:34:12.770
I'll keep on walking, as long as I live!

01:34:18.410 --> 01:34:21.150
Back to Ryoko...

01:34:21.150 --> 01:34:23.050
Back to Japan!

01:35:22.580 --> 01:35:25.070
Devil!

01:35:27.720 --> 01:35:31.120
Will you still order me to kill people?!

01:35:31.120 --> 01:35:34.720
Did you guide me here so you could
make me a killer?!

01:35:34.720 --> 01:35:38.890
Am I supposed to live on by
taking people's lives?!

01:35:47.740 --> 01:35:51.200
In order to get out of Area 88,

01:35:51.840 --> 01:35:55.680
a pilot must survive three years of combat,

01:35:56.280 --> 01:35:59.510
pay a penalty of 1.5 million dollars,

01:36:00.250 --> 01:36:04.810
or he can desert.

01:36:14.530 --> 01:36:17.870
Sono te wo nobashite
<i>Hold out your hand</i>

01:36:17.870 --> 01:36:21.340
Watashi wo kanjite
<i>Sense my presence</i>

01:36:21.340 --> 01:36:27.110
Kokoro wa soba ni aru kara
<i>In spirit, I am by your side</i>

01:36:27.940 --> 01:36:31.180
Kuchibiru kasanete
<i>Put your lips to mine</i>

01:36:31.180 --> 01:36:40.260
Tsukareta karada wo yasashiku tsutsunde ageru
<i>I will tenderly embrace your weary body</i>

01:36:40.260 --> 01:36:46.500
Close your eyes to surely find
Close your eyes to surely find

01:36:46.500 --> 01:36:50.900
The memory of love
The memory of love

01:36:51.730 --> 01:36:57.470
Kimagure ni kawaru sadame sae
<i>Even fickle fate</i>

01:36:58.310 --> 01:37:03.210
Ai made ubaenai
<i>Cannot steal love</i>

01:37:03.210 --> 01:37:06.450
Love is light in the dark
Love is light in the dark

01:37:06.450 --> 01:37:10.220
Show the way like stars
Show the way like stars

01:37:10.220 --> 01:37:16.330
Ima wa munashiku kizutsuite mo
<i>Even though right now you've been hurt in vain</i>

01:37:16.330 --> 01:37:19.660
Love is force in your mind
Love is force in your mind

01:37:19.660 --> 01:37:23.300
Wash away lonely tears
Wash away lonely tears

01:37:23.300 --> 01:37:29.500
Mirai katareru sono hi made
<i>Until that day when you're ready to speak of the future</i>

01:37:36.980 --> 01:37:40.280
Ashita wo sagashite
<i>Seek tomorrow</i>

01:37:40.280 --> 01:37:43.490
Inochi wo moyashite
Blaze with life

01:37:43.490 --> 01:37:49.260
Kokoro mo utsurou hito yo
Oh, you whose heart is vacant

01:37:49.260 --> 01:37:55.300
Close your eyes to surely find
Close your eyes to surely find

01:37:55.300 --> 01:37:59.930
The memory of love
The memory of love
